From 6cfafba540a8a9b3430744ccb298e6dfd6cf8672 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Bradley <eric@basepowercompany.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 20:05:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: can: mcan: ignore Tx events for completed Tx Buffers

When a Tx Event FIFO new entry (IR.TEFN) and a bus-off state change are
pending in the same pass of can_mcan_line_0_isr(), the state change
handler runs first and completes every Tx Buffer with -ENETUNREACH,
clearing its callback. The Tx event handler then reads the event of a
frame that was transmitted before bus-off and calls the cleared, NULL,
callback.

Skip Tx events whose Tx Buffer no longer has a callback. The event is
still acknowledged, and tx_sem is no longer given a second time for the
same Tx Buffer.

Reproduced on an STM32G431 by masking the FDCAN interrupts while a
transmitted frame's Tx event is pending and the controller goes bus-off.

Fixes #121845

Assisted-by: Amp:claude-opus-5.5
Signed-off-by: Eric Bradley <eric@basepowercompany.com>
---
 drivers/can/can_mcan.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/can/can_mcan.c b/drivers/can/can_mcan.c
index baf974adb3b1e..40a5eb0647979 100644
--- a/drivers/can/can_mcan.c
+++ b/drivers/can/can_mcan.c
@@ -568,12 +568,16 @@ static void can_mcan_tx_event_handler(const struct device *dev)
 
 		__ASSERT_NO_MSG(tx_idx < cbs->num_tx);
 		tx_cb = cbs->tx[tx_idx].function;
-		user_data = cbs->tx[tx_idx].user_data;
-		cbs->tx[tx_idx].function = NULL;
 
-		k_sem_give(&data->tx_sem);
+		/* The bus-off handler may already have completed this Tx Buffer */
+		if (tx_cb != NULL) {
+			user_data = cbs->tx[tx_idx].user_data;
+			cbs->tx[tx_idx].function = NULL;
 
-		tx_cb(dev, 0, user_data);
+			k_sem_give(&data->tx_sem);
+
+			tx_cb(dev, 0, user_data);
+		}
 
 		err = can_mcan_read_reg(dev, CAN_MCAN_TXEFS, &txefs);
 		if (err != 0) {
